      "widgets_values": [
        "A weathered brass diving helmet resting on wet black basalt at the tideline, pre-dawn, heavy overcast. Cold blue-grey ambient light with a single warm sodium lamp somewhere off-frame throwing a thin amber edge along the rim. Salt haze in the air; the whole palette stays desaturated except that one amber accent.\n\nThe shot begins exactly on the first image: the helmet upright and closed, seawater beading on the glass port, the tide still low. The camera holds, then begins a slow arcing dolly to the left at a constant rate, never cutting. As it moves, the tide rises steadily around the base, foam threading between the rocks; condensation inside the faceplate slowly clears from the centre outward. The sodium edge-light creeps further across the brass as the angle changes. The movement resolves precisely on the composition of the last image.\n\nAudio: low ocean swell with a long slow period, water draining through rock crevices between waves, occasional distant buoy bell, faint metallic resonance from the helmet as water reaches it, and a soft rising drone that fades out in the final second.",
        864,
        480,
        124
