      "flags": {},
      "order": 90,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "### Sol-Attn tuning\n\nBlock-sparse attention. Measured on a 3090 vs SageAttention 2.2:\n**3.2x at 12k tokens, 4.0x at 32k**.\n\n- **tau** — sparsity. Higher = faster, less accurate.\n  `1.2` -> density ~0.125. Range `1.0-1.5` is speed-first; drop to `0.6-0.8` if you see artifacts.\n- **min_seq_len** — below this, falls through to normal attention (SageAttention wins under ~8k).\n- **preserve_prefix_blocks** — force-keeps the first N 128-token blocks. H3 packs the sequence as\n  `[text | cond | audio | video]`, so this protects the text prefix. `0` is speed-first; try `8-16`\n  if prompt adherence degrades.\n- **log_every** — logs measured density to console.\n\n**Check the `Sol-Attn Stats` node after a run.** If `sol_attn=0` it never engaged (raise resolution\nor lower `min_seq_len`). If `last_density` > 0.35 there is little speedup — raise `tau`.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
